  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready, with six questions on O4 (workflows versus agents, and who owns the control flow). The quiz is in `quizzes/0002.json` and the key is in `keys/0002.json`.\n\n- **What it covers:** the defining difference between a workflow and an agent, and classifying a design. It also covers a cost calculation, spotting which makerspace task suits a fixed workflow, what an agent can do that a workflow can't, and a design-review decision about how to split the assistant.\n- **Format:** four multiple-choice items, one numeric item and one short-answer item. The examples come from the makerspace assistant, and the difficulty rises toward the design-review question.\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** no lesson covers O4 yet, so I wrote the quiz from the wording of the objective alone, without a lesson or a searched source. I didn't search for or cite a high-trust source, which the guide suggests when there's no lesson. The key's rationales come from my own reasoning, so check them against a source if you plan to rely on them.\n- **Misconception ids:** the workspace has no misconception ids for O4 yet, so I left `distractors` out of the key.\n- **Checks:** I answered each item from its stem alone and each had a single defensible answer.\n\nWould you like a lesson on O4 before you take the quiz?",
